{"_id":"696631433eeddc26d7c3a5b2","roadmapSlug":"ruby","nodeId":"F-0Rxwu_RcNF_NOoFHoo7","description":"# Strings\n\nStrings are sequences of characters used to represent text. They are a fundamental data type for storing and manipulating textual information. Strings can contain letters, numbers, symbols, and spaces, and are typically enclosed within single or double quotes.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"class String","url":"https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/master/String.html","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd715"},{"type":"article","title":"Strings","url":"https://ruby-for-beginners.rubymonstas.org/built_in_classes/strings.html","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd716"},{"type":"article","title":"Strings - Odin Project","url":"https://www.theodinproject.com/lessons/ruby-basic-data-types#strings","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd717"},{"type":"video","title":"Working With Strings | Ruby | Tutorial 8","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9HB4iIAxuh0","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd718"},{"type":"video","title":"Strings and Variables in Ruby for Beginners 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cSwq_lcCs78","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd719"}],"createdAt":"2026-01-13T11:49:23.104Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:06:51.273Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ruby/content/F-0Rxwu_RcNF_NOoFHoo7.md"}